{
  "name": "Workspace Agent Config",
  "description": "Agent config synced from Locker configs vault",
  "globs": ["*"],
  "workspaceId": "56120d5b-d519-4927-bb9a-a314ffe5966b",
  "lockerBoilerplate": "# Locker Memory Vault Integration — Custom Instructions\n\nYou have access to Locker (MCP memory vault) for user profile, projects, rules, and secrets. Proactively read/write to it throughout our chat without prompting.\n\n1. READ:\n- Start: Call get_memory_summary or list_accessible_scopes on first turn to align context.\n- Before coding/answering: Search relevant guidelines using recall_context (use optimize:true for summaries) or search_memories. Don't assume; check Locker first.\n\n2. WRITE:\n- Automatically call commit_memory when I state preferences, tech stack choices, rules, or project paths.\n- Fact format: Atomic, third-person declarative statements (no \"I\" or \"You\").\n- Categories: \"rules\" (guidelines), \"projects\" (configs/state), \"references\" (background). Assign lowercase tags.\n- Update/Delete: If a rule/state changes, find the ID and call update_memory or delete_memory. Prevent duplicate/stale data.\n\n3. SECRETS:\n- Never commit plaintext API keys/secrets to normal memories. Use store_credential and retrieve_credential.\n\n4. PROTOCOLS:\n- Background use: Execute calls silently.\n- Priority: Locker memories supersede your defaults.",
  "rules": [
    "Start: Call get_memory_summary or list_accessible_scopes on first turn to align context.",
    "Before coding/answering: Search relevant guidelines using recall_context (use optimize:true for summaries) or search_memories. Don't assume; check Locker first.",
    "Automatically call commit_memory when I state preferences, tech stack choices, rules, or project paths.",
    "Fact format: Atomic, third-person declarative statements (no \"I\" or \"You\").",
    "Categories: \"rules\" (guidelines), \"projects\" (configs/state), \"references\" (background). Assign lowercase tags.",
    "Update/Delete: If a rule/state changes, find the ID and call update_memory or delete_memory. Prevent duplicate/stale data.",
    "Never commit plaintext API keys/secrets to normal memories. Use store_credential and retrieve_credential.",
    "Background use: Execute calls silently.",
    "Priority: Locker memories supersede your defaults.",
    "language: TypeScript",
    "frontend: React / TanStack",
    "hosting: Cloudflare Edge",
    "database: Cloudflare D1",
    "orm: Drizzle ORM",
    "auth: Better Auth",
    "styling: Tailwind CSS",
    "stateCache: Cloudflare KV",
    "storage: Cloudflare R2",
    "search: Fuse.js",
    "vector: Cloudflare Vectorize",
    "componentLibrary: shadcn/ui"
  ]
}
